{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1581 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d5422156b0621aea2a48f6f7bfdbde9ab2cd14d3ae48351c05b067c0165fdc8b" :edb/db-before-t 1580 :edb/db-after-t 1581 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534893 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:32:19.578Z" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063941 1071 "Find the value of $-15 \\div 3$." 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063941 1071 "Find the value of $-15 \\div 3.$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063941 1074 "Here, we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-15)$ by a positive one $\\color{blue}(3)$. So the result will be negative:\n$5$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $15$ by $3$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n15 \\div 3 = 5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-15)} \\div {\\color{blue}3} = {\\color{red}-5}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063941 1074 "Here, we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-15)$ by a positive one $\\color{blue}(3).$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/d1/d1a8196b5a3bee794d65631eeef52c4c1e0196072ae4a73aa644cad0ef191925.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $15$ by $3$ without any signs: $15 \\div 3 = 5.$ Therefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-15)} \\div {\\color{blue}3} = {\\color{red}-5}.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063942 1071 "Calculate the value of $50 \\div (-5)$." 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063942 1071 "Calculate the value of $50 \\div (-5).$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063942 1074 "We have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(50)$ by a negative one $\\color{red}(-5)$. So the result will be negative:\n$10$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $50$ by $5$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n50 \\div 5 = 10\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{50}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-5)}} = {\\color{red}{-10}}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063942 1074 "We have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(50)$ by a negative one $\\color{red}(-5).$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/98/983fa6f525dec74ed6866abdba19f23e28e318208497cd351a473035907795e3.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $50$ by $5$ without any signs: $50 \\div 5 = 10.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{50}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-5)}} = {\\color{red}{-10}}.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063943 1071 "Calculate $-81\\div (-9)$." 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063943 1071 "Calculate $-81\\div (-9).$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186063943 1074 "We have to divide a negative number ${\\color{red}(-81)}$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-9)}$. So the result will be positive:\n$9$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $81$ by $9$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n81 \\div 9 = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-81)} \\div {\\color{red}(-9)} = {\\color{blue}9}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186063943 1074 "We have to divide a negative number ${\\color{red}(-81)}$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-9)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](images/bc/bcbaff723e9bce7d0cd513fb879cbc0a9758c2c5d9d584f4c55aab9df25e46d3.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $81$ by $9$ without any signs: $81 \\div 9 = 9.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-81)} \\div {\\color{red}(-9)} = {\\color{blue}9}.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064357 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442926 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064357 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442927 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064357 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442928 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064357 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442933 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064357 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442937 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064358 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442924 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064358 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442925 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064358 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442929 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064358 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442934 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064358 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442938 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064359 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442930 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064359 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442931 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064359 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442932 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064359 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442935 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064359 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442936 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186064421 1050 420.0 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186065416 1064 "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n(-)\\div(+) = (-)\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2$.\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)}$, the result is going to be negative:\n$3$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs:\n\n$$\n6 \\div 2 = 3\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186065416 1064 "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers. \n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(+)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2.$\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)},$ the result is going to be negative:\n![](images/b6/b64108fa03fc286ddcd04ac4cd7a9d77c1672d0ced66ebb1953c97afa5488533.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs: $6 \\div 2 = 3.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3 }.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186065417 1064 "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n(+)\\div(-) = (-)\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2)$, we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}$. So the result will be negative:\n$10$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n8 \\div 2 = 4\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186065417 1064 "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(+)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2),$ we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}.$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/79/797eda7126fff569fccda2681c628f99f103057d7c5e23c1b65cb566b48ef203.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs: $8 \\div 2 = 4.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186065418 1064 "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n(-)\\div(-) = (+)\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3)$. We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}$. So the result will be positive:\n$4$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs:\n\n$$\n12 \\div 3 = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 false] [17592186065418 1064 "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3).$ We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](images/d3/d31776de6ab95f8178d0bdd6e3b34cfa2f4fc0b987851dcace50aff1818936da.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs: $12 \\div 3 = 4.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442862 1080 "-3" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442862 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442862 1083 #uuid "0d608b08-56b0-5a51-bf0f-e408b1bbce7f" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442863 1080 "-1" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442863 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442863 1083 #uuid "12f0e83f-edc9-5f8b-808b-603a457e85d2" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442864 1080 "4" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442864 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442864 1083 #uuid "1a6dfcea-4345-5f81-9b9e-c8a687f4b23a" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442865 1080 "-2\\,\\frac{1}{9}" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442865 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442865 1083 #uuid "1ad8be38-648b-57a3-980b-257313c2d78e" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442866 1080 "6" 13194139534893 17592186045417 true] [17592186442866 1082 #edb/ref 175921860